  "solution": {
    "text": "Since resistance connected in arms <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">CE</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"italic\"> ED</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"italic\"> CF</mi></math><br />and <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">FD</mi></math> will form a balanced Wheatstone bridge,<br />therefore, the resistance of arm <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">EF</mi></math> becomes<br />ineffective. Now resistance of arm <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">CED</mi></math> or <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">CFD</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br />Effective resistance of these two parallel arm <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><br />Now resistance of arm <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">ACDB</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br />in parallel with resistance arm <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">AB</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> Thus,<br />effective resistance between <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><br />&nbsp;"
  }
